# Veritas writes its last-failed list, lcov and JUnit output here.
reports/

# A secret is encrypted before it is a file at all, and the encrypted
# copies live outside the checkout (~/.config/wolk-jjba/secrets).  These
# two lines are the belt to that braces: if WOLK_JJBA_SECRETS_LOCAL is
# ever pointed inside the tree, or a token is saved as .gpg next to the
# code, git still refuses to carry it.  A test fixture that has to be
# committed needs another name (.asc, or a directory of its own).
secrets/
*.gpg
